#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""sen0414_lineage_brief_exam9 v1_0_0 - brief r14 for TK4_Papers: the r10 brief plus the inputs that now exist (engine v1_1_0, item sets A 2.1.0 and B 2.0.0, cover renderer, design v1_2_0) and what the renderer must measure. New file in 08-tooling/briefs/exam/r14."""
__version__ = "1.0.0"
import os
here = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)); out = os.path.join(here, "briefs/exam/r14"); os.makedirs(out, exist_ok=True)
ADD = """## What exists now and what this task builds on (r14; controlled by the lineage agent; these replace anything in the brief below that says otherwise)
1. ENGINE `04-assessment/exams/exam_engine_v1_1_0.py` (commit 540b51b), design `04-assessment/exams/exam_design_v1_2_0.json`. Command: `exam_engine_v1_1_0.py build --pool POOL.json --design DESIGN.json --seed N --out DIR [--kind midterm|makeup] [--midterm MIDTERM_BUILD.json]`. It writes, per seed and kind, `*_paper.json` (the blocks of forms A and B for the renderer), `*_key.json`, `*_sheetspec.json` (the sheet specification in the format of the SEN0401 sheet module), `*_build.json` (the verdict of E01 to E28 and the constants), `*_authored.json`, `*_buildfull.json`. Read the engine file and these outputs; do not edit the engine.
2. ITEMS. Pools are one named set per paper, merged by id: paper pool = `items/items_a_v2_1_0.json` + `items/items_b_v2_0_0.json`; make-up pool = `items/items_a_v2_1_0_makeup.json` + `items/items_b_v2_0_0_makeup.json`, each written as `{"sets": [{"name": "paper", "items": [...]}]}` (and `"makeup"`); the make-up is built with `--kind makeup --midterm` of the paper's build record (otherwise E17 compares nothing). The lineage agent's builds of both pools pass 28 of 28 rules (seeds 1, 20261101, 20261102 for the paper). Items are PROVISIONAL (the Owner's question styles have not arrived): your renderer must work for any pool that builds.
3. COVER `04-assessment/exams/exam_cover_v1_0_0.py` (commit bea6a20, controlled): reuse it for page 1; the Owner's template stays outside the repository and is never committed.
4. ANSWER SHEET: the SEN0401 sheet module, reused and never edited, driven by the engine's `*_sheetspec.json`; a position-exact PDF. The engine's layout figures (95 characters a line, a 92 per cent spare share of the last question page) are ASSUMPTIONS: your renderer must MEASURE the real pages and report the real numbers and whether 4 pages (or the allowed 6) hold, and if not, which question breaks the budget. If it does not fit in 6 pages, STOP and report; do not shrink the text below readable size.
5. FORMS: build the midterm paper forms A and B (seed 20261102 unless you have a reason) and the make-up form A, as .docx (paper and key) and the sheet PDFs; the dates and the form letter go on the cover; the keys must agree with the engine's key data (your check recomputes the key from the .docx text and compares).
6. THE CHECK is a new file with fixtures of known answer: it opens each .docx, counts questions, sub-questions and options, finds every tip and every abbreviation at first use, confirms code listings are monospace and unwrapped, confirms the key against the engine's key data, and converts to PDF with LibreOffice only to count pages (CANNOT_RUN if it is not installed; say so). Render pages to images and read them; report what you saw.
"""
t = open(os.path.join(here, "briefs/exam/r10/BRIEF_TK4_Papers.md"), encoding="utf-8").read(); head = t.split("\n\n")[0]
i = t.index("\n\n") + 2
open(os.path.join(out, "BRIEF_TK4_Papers.md"), "w", encoding="utf-8").write(head + "\n\nTask TK4_Papers (written by the lineage agent for the exam change of 2026-11-01). Estimated 2.5 hours of agent work (an estimate, G120).\n\nDepends on: TK4_Engine5_Verify, TK4_Cover_Verify, TK4_Items_A2_Verify, TK4_Items_A3_Verify, TK4_Items_B2_Verify (all Done once the lineage agent has registered them)\n\n" + ADD + "\n" + t[i:].split("\n\n", 1)[1]); print("wrote")
